Module Std.Files

== Definitions of text files (canon r3.58 module pair: Std.Files defines,
== Std.IOUtils works; OpenSpec change file-io).
==
== The type File is a compiler intrinsic, visible in a program that uses
== Std.Files or Std.IOUtils.
==
==   File     == an open text file, owned by the routine that holds it.
==
== Rules of a File (F1, F6):
==   - it is closed when the routine that holds it exits by any path: the
==     end, Return, Exit or an exception; Close(F) closes it earlier, and
==     closing twice does nothing;
==   - it is never copied: it is a local variable that receives a file just
==     opened (F := OpenRead(Path)), or a ref mut parameter. It cannot be a
==     struct field, an array element, a State variable or a result, and it
==     cannot be compared.
==
== The errors of file operations are the exception types of Std.Errors:
== FileNotFound, PermissionDenied, AlreadyExists and DiskFull, all kinds of
== IOError, which is raised for any other failure.
